$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-Trifluoroacetyl 2-Methylbenzenesulfonamide (13b).
2-Methylbenzenesulfonamide (5 mmol, 885 mg) was added a mixture of TFA
(1.3 equiv, 910 μL) in toluene (15 mL), and the reaction mixture was
heated to reflux and monitored by LC-MS until all of the starting
material was consumed completely. Solvent was removed in vacuo, the
residue was diluted with 30 mL of ethyl acetate and washed with 30 mL
water, and then the organic phase was washed with brine and dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4. The organic layer was concentrated. A white solid
without further purification (1.268 g, 95%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
8.81 (s, 1H), 8.21 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.62-7.58 (m, 1H), 7.44 (t, J =
7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 2.68 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (150 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 138.4, 135.3, 135.0, 133.0, 132.1, 126.9, 58.7, 20.5, 18.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Benzofused Five-Ring Sultams via Rh-Catalyzed C-H
Olefination Directed by an N-Ac-Substituted Sulfonamide Group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Xueyuan; Dong, Yi; Qu, Fengyu; Liu, Gang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2015), 80(2), 790-798

